A||||6||DR650SE||any easy oil leak fixes?||||4||
Z||000000||DR650SE||11-13-2001||06:25 PM||||My oil seems to be leaking in two maybe three places pretty slow.  I havnt been able to look where because I am pretty busy.  Also This is a really good engine and I don't want to damage it.  It is also my daily driver.  Is there anything I can do thats easy or cheap to fix this?  This would expain the low pressure in turns.  Any help is appreciated.  <P>------------------<BR>AIM:  DR650SE<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||4
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||11-13-2001||06:46 PM||||Replacing the correct gaskets or seals is about the only 'easy' way to take care of the problem that I know of.<BR>Low oil pressure in turns?||||reg||1
Z||000002||DR650SE||11-13-2001||07:03 PM||||Low pressure light turned on when i made a hard turn.  as time went on the easy turns triggered it to.  I think because i had less and less oil in the car I think it was because the oil all went to one side of the pan and starved the oil pump.  I really really don't want to damage anything, I can't afford it now.  Also what grade of oil do i use on a v6?  Is it 5w-30? Thanks for any info||||reg||1
Z||000003||DR650SE||11-13-2001||07:04 PM||||Low pressure light turned on when i made a hard turn.  as time went on the easy turns triggered it to.  I think because i had less and less oil in the car I think it was because the oil all went to one side of the pan and starved the oil pump.  I really really don't want to damage anything, I can't afford it now.  Also what grade of oil do i use on a v6?  Is it 5w-30? Thanks for any info.  How many quarts of oil too?  Sorry if this posted 2 times||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfiero||11-13-2001||08:47 PM||||If you drain the oil then you will have no leaks!   j/k   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>If the leaks are pretty slow then you can keep tabs on things fairly easily......just carry a couple of quarts of oil in the trunk and check the level eveyday.<P>Otherwise, change the gaskets where the leaks are (if easily accessible) and go from there.<P>Where is it leaking from?  The most common places are the valve covers (also includes the PCV grommets), oil pan, cam cover (underneath timing chain cover), distributor O ring.<P>If it's the oil pan you can help things by tightening up the bolts that you can access......it won't cure things, but it might help (sometimes the bolts are pretty loose).  The distributor O ring is the most common failure......it is an easy fix, but you must carefully mark the position of the distributor before removing it, otherwise you'll need to re-set the timing.<BR> <BR>GM recommends using 5W-30, which is what I use, but 10W-30 or 10W-40 will be OK as well.   <P>Good luck!||||reg||10
Z||000005||Jake_Dragon||11-13-2001||09:42 PM||||I run 10w50 in the summer, will be changing to 10w40 for the winter, as soon as it gets here  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||DR650SE||11-13-2001||11:05 PM||||Thanks all for the info.  I appreiciate it.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>AIM:  DR650SE<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||1
